{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nOn 2026-09-07 eleven forgotten vig instances, each re-fetching its Projects board every five minutes and polling the GitHub page, exhausted the account's 5,000 GraphQL points/hour again and again — and an exhausted quota takes every `gh` invocation on the account down with it.\n\n## Spec\n\n1. **Idle backoff** — ten minutes without a key press puts automatic refreshes into idle mode: the Projects stale re-fetch goes from 5 to 30 minutes, the GitHub page's run / jobs / watch polling to 6× `github-poll-interval` (capped at 10 minutes). Any key press restores the normal cadence at once; the status bar shows `idle`.\n2. **Re-check the disk cache before fetching** — right before a stale re-fetch, re-read the cache file's mtime: if another instance refreshed it within the threshold, reload it instead of fetching. N parallel instances then fetch effectively once per five minutes.\n3. **Quota-aware throttling** — piggy-back `rateLimit { remaining }` on the GitHub page's stacks query as well as the Projects views query (both cost 0) and show the remaining points in the shared header (warning below 1,500). Below 20 % remaining, double every automatic interval; below 5 %, stop automatic refreshes entirely (manual `r` only, with the reason in the status bar).\n4. **Local cache for REST polling** — `gh api --cache 30s` on the run / jobs / check-runs polls, so a repeated request for the same URL within the window never leaves the machine.\n5. **Kill switch** — top-level `github-auto-refresh \"on\" | \"off\"` (default `on`); `off` leaves only manual `r`. Documented in the Config Reference and Troubleshooting.\n\n## Tests\n\nIdle detection and interval arithmetic, the cache-mtime fetch skip, the per-threshold intervals, and `github-auto-refresh` validation.\n\n## Context\n\nMeasured on 2026-09-07 (#163): a board fetch costs ~50 points after the limit reduction, issue / PR lists and details ~0; the burn came purely from the number of instances × cadence.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-08T08:11:36Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":168,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Stop idle and duplicate vig instances from burning the GitHub quota"}
